  "page1": {
    "title": "The Heartbeat of Korean Music",
    "subtitle": "Four drums and gongs make the strong beat of samulnori.",
    "body": "Korean music has a long and proud story. We call this old music <u>gugak</u>. It is full of strong and lively beats.\n\nOne famous part of gugak is samulnori. Four players sit close together on the floor. Each one holds a special drum or gong.\n\nThe kkwaenggwari is a small brass gong. It rings a sharp, high sound. The jing is a big, wide gong. It makes a deep and long sound.\n\nThe janggu is an hourglass drum with two heads. The buk is a round barrel drum. Together they <mark>keep the beat</mark> as one.\n\nThis steady beat is called jangdan. The music starts slow and then grows fast. People clap their hands and feel the heartbeat of Korea.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/10.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Four players with the kkwaenggwari, jing, janggu, and buk, keeping the beat of samulnori."
  },
